% Lesson 8a (minicourse-evaluation.org) - unfolding cuts a cycle.
%
% pro derives B from an obligation for A, back derives A from an
% obligation for B.  Unfolded for B, the demand for B inside back meets a
% statement that is already being expanded and has no binder in scope
% (pro's binders are continuations for B, i.e. B[c]), so it stays the
% bare site ?u3:B.
lk.
declare A,B:bool.
declare r1: (A -> B).
declare r3: (B -> A).

argument pro : (B).
cut (A -> B) th.
axiom r1.
elim.
next.
axiom.
dixi.

argument back : (A).
cut (B -> A) th.
axiom r3.
elim.
next.
axiom.
dixi.

graph document.
